\begin{center}
{\large{\textbf{Homework 7}}}
\end{center}

\begin{enumerate}
  
  \item \textbf{Pig Pens: CRD vs Nesting}.
  The dataset \texttt{pig_feed_data.csv} in Canvas contains (synthetic) data from the following experiment:
  
  \begin{quote}
    An agricultural researcher would like to test the impact new feed formulations will impact swine weight.
    They have three formulas they would like to compare, and access to 60 pigs.
    They group together the pigs in pens of 5 pigs each, given 12 total pens.
    They then perform a completely randomized design, assigning each of the three distinct feed formulas to four pens each, and measure the weight of the pigs after 1 month. 
  \end{quote}

\end{enumerate}


